course: dictionary
lesson: 14063
title: Matched: put together, or made equal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Matched has a few meanings, but they all link to one idea: two things that go together, or two things that are the same. «She matched each sock with its pair.» Here matched means put together with the thing that goes with it.
explain: «His dad matched what he saved.» Matched here means made the same, so his dad put in the same amount of money. Think of it as equal, the same on both sides.
explain: Matched can also describe things. «Two well-matched teams played all afternoon.» Well-matched means the teams are about as good as each other. Look at the words around matched to find which meaning fits.
fact: Matched means put together with something that goes with it, or made the same as something.
fact: Matched is the past of the verb match: she matched the colours.
fact: Well-matched means about as good as each other.
fact: In maths, pairs made from things: if you have 6 pairs of gloves, you have 12 gloves, because 6 times 2 is 12.
fact: «Matched his savings» can mean he added the same amount again, so the total doubled.
exercise: «She matched each sock with its pair.» What does matched mean here? | *Put together with the thing that goes with it | Thrown in the bin | Washed in hot water | Lost
exercise: «His dad matched what he saved.» What does matched mean here? | Spent all of it | Lost it in the park | Hid it under the bed | *Made the same, so equal
exercise: «Two well-matched teams played all afternoon.» What does well-matched mean? | Tired and wet | Much better than the other team | Very different from each other | *About as good as each other
test: «The shop matched every pound a child gave to the charity.» What does matched mean here? | Kept the money for the shop | *Gave the same amount again | Took away a pound | Counted the coins twice
test: If you have 6 pairs of gloves, how many gloves do you have? | 6 | 8 | *12 | 3
exam: What does matched mean in «The two well-matched dancers moved in time»? | Put in a box | Lost in the crowd | *About equal in skill | Painted in bright colours
